{
  "dom_id": "step-20084",
  "name": "The Number of Real Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix",
  "problem": "The characteristic equation of any $2 \\!\\times\\! 2$ matrix $A$ is always a quadratic equation, which implies that $A$ has at most $2$ eigenvalues. Here are the all possible cases:\n\n- Two distinct real eigenvalues\n\n- One repeated real eigenvalue (or, equivalently, two real eigenvalues that are the same)\n\n- No real eigenvalues (or, equivalently, two complex eigenvalues)",
